1
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,540
Floating on the Nakagawa,
aiming for the setting sun

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and
my shoes went flying too

3
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:32,940
onto the head of the
carpenter who'd been saving up

4
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:39,140
They laughed that I was still just a kid

5
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I deliver some energy somewhere

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:47,460
Katsushika Kameari, even yawns are unusual

7
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:53,160
The unused streetscape is strangely gentle

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,160
From the pointed roof of the water basin

9
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:07,440
The sunset falls toward the shrine hall

10
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:15,900
Tomorrow will end like this too, won't it

11
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:21,020
Katsushika Shibamata, even happiness is lost

12
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,600
I only realized it after hearing,
because I'm such a fool

13
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,420
Ninja old man

14
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:37,020
H-hey, I'm kinda getting excited

15
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:40,940
Even though you have Jodie,
is this okay, you lady-killer?

16
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:45,120
Well, I don't think there's a
woman better than Jodie, though

17
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,440
You never know, just in case

18
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,880
Yeah, go ahead and open it

19
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,280
Alright, then

20
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:59,160
I thought my eyes were going to rot.

21
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:00,660
Help me.

22
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:03,700
I don't want to have a marriage
meeting with someone like this.

23
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:08,820
Why don't you just turn it down by
saying you already have a fiancée?

24
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:11,120
I already said that when the
marriage meeting offer came in.

25
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:14,180
And then Grandpa said to bring her along.

26
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,900
Then why don't you just bring Jodie?

27
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:23,460
But she's out on naval exercises right now,
so I can't get in touch with her.

28
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:27,640
Besides, she won't let me marry
her unless I beat her in a fight.

29
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:29,780
Please, do something about it.

30
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:33,240
At this rate,
I'll be forced to marry this Miyaya woman.

31
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,820
Well, I could do something about it,
but it won't be free, you know.

32
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,780
I'll pay whatever it takes.

33
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:41,160
Leave it to me.

34
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:45,920
Ninja?

35
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:48,720
So you're a ninja?

36
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:50,706
We've been like that for generations, so

37
00:02:50,756 --> 00:02:54,340
Grandpa plans to marry me
off and make me his heir.

38
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:56,220
Of course,
I have no intention of inheriting it, but

39
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:58,260
You're in the same situation I am.

40
00:02:58,260 --> 00:02:59,938
Well, that's how it is, so

41
00:02:59,988 --> 00:03:03,300
Make sure you pass yourself off
well as Volvo's fiancée, Maria.

42
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,820
Yes, I'll do my best!

43
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:05,980
Nice to meet you.

44
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,160
That's my family home.

45
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:10,580
Mm, it really looks the part.

46
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,080
It really looks like a ninja might pop out.

47
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:14,180
Yeah.

48
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,160
Nobody's home

49
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,660
You can tell without even going inside?

50
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,220
When there's a red ribbon tied on,
it means they're out.

51
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:25,980
Over there.

52
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:28,900
They should've left a stone marker showing where they went,
probably.

53
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:29,560
Stones?

54
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:32,640
Even the Boy Scouts use stone signals.

55
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:33,680
Like this.

56
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,440
It's like a ninja's.

57
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:37,420
Found it!

58
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,380
Looks like they went shopping.

59
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:46,380
Easy to figure out, right?

60
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,000
Nobody's home, so there's nothing we can do.

61
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,300
Guess we'll wait inside.

62
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:52,580
Wait a second.

63
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:54,080
Here.

64
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:57,480
Just as I thought.

65
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,200
Grandpa's super cautious.

66
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,840
He's set traps all over
to keep out intruders.

67
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:04,200
Get caught in one of those and you'd die,
you know.

68
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:04,780
Idiot.

69
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:06,640
If I'm going to say anything,
it's to Grandpa.

70
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:09,040
Lead the way.

71
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:11,260
So, you knew about this?

72
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:12,360
Magnificent!

73
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:17,620
Grandpa

74
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:19,380
What is this

75
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:21,140
But why are you dressed as Komusou?

76
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:24,780
You're going shopping dressed
in such an old-fashioned getup.

77
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:28,600
I'm dressed inconspicuously so
no one will know I'm a ninja.

78
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:31,340
That outfit is way more conspicuous,
you know!

79
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,200
But you often see that in period dramas.

80
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:41,160
So this woman is the
one I'm supposed to marry?

81
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:41,640
Yes.

82
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:43,380
This is Ai Asou.

83
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:44,260
She's huge!

84
00:04:48,080 --> 00:05:15,620
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

85
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:16,440
Well, come inside.

86
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:21,440
What are you doing?

87
00:05:27,420 --> 00:05:28,760
I see, what an elaborate trap.

88
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:29,960
Follow me.

89
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:36,720
Hey, you could just walk on the ground,
so why bother walking on the logs?

90
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:40,660
Gramps values tradition and atmosphere,
you see.

91
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:43,660
How nostalgic. This is my room.

92
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:46,440
My room!

93
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,700
I turned it into a ninja museum.

94
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:54,840
Without permission, how could you just...

95
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:57,560
We charge admission for
people to come see it.

96
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,600
And it's not just a museum.

97
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:03,220
Next spring, I plan to open a ninja school.

98
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:04,500
A ninja school?

99
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:08,240
We'll rake in a fortune by attracting
crowds of students from home and abroad.

100
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,900
Let me go change quickly, so wait here.

101
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,980
There's even a souvenir corner!

102
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:19,240
Ugh, Grandpa's autographed photos!

103
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:22,320
He even has videos where he
stars and books he's written.

104
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:25,940
Grandpa's shakuhachi.

105
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,380
What's this?

106
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:31,120
It's a tape. It's a fake, isn't it?

107
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:35,860
Don't touch things without permission,
Grandpa.

108
00:06:35,860 --> 00:06:37,580
Honestly, you're such a dangerous guy.

109
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:40,020
Just what you'd expect from Volvo's grandpa.

110
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,740
But you look so cool in that ninja getup.

111
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,160
Really, it's lovely.

112
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:48,880
Heh heh, you think so?
Well, do sit back and have some tea.

113
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,460
Here you go,
herbal tea that's good for your body.

114
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:52,060
Oh my.

115
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:53,161
However,

116
00:06:53,211 --> 00:06:57,160
One of these supposedly has an
herb that gives you diarrhea?

117
00:06:57,340 --> 00:07:01,260
We were made to do poison-tolerance
training like that since we were kids.

118
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,800
It's like Russian roulette!

119
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:05,980
Well, this one's mine.

120
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:07,680
Ryo-sama?

121
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,840
Mm, mm, delicious! This one's the dud!

122
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:13,460
Gramps, that was the one, wasn't it?

123
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,980
Yep, jackpot.

124
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:20,020
What?! What are you gonna do about this?!
We drank it, you idiot!

125
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:23,280
Don't worry. It's called shinobi medicine.

126
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,200
Ninjas are well versed in
all sorts of medicinal herbs.

127
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:27,730
Salves, styptics, and the like,

128
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:30,540
we make them by mixing
all kinds of herbs together.

129
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:35,980
First, we grind the herbs in this mortar,
grind, grind, grind, grind, grind, grind...

130
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:43,160
Grind it up. Brew it, brew it, brew it.

131
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,680
Brew it, brew it, brew it, brew it.

132
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:48,820
There, it's done.

133
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:51,980
It's ninja secret decoction.
This'll cure you right up.

134
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:52,540
Give it here!

135
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,940
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

136
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,460
That'll be 1,500 yen.

137
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:58,620
That's way too expensive!

138
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:01,280
Then enjoy your diarrhea.

139
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:05,280
Fine, fine. I'll pay.

140
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:06,560
Here you go.

141
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:08,920
Thanks for your business!

142
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:15,820
What a greedy old geezer.

143
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:17,520
What did you say?

144
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:23,500
Master, throwing shuriken around
inside the room like that is dangerous!

145
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:26,600
Right, step outside. A one-on-one duel!

146
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,460
Bring it on.

147
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:28,580
Milady.

148
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:29,600
Senpai.

149
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,220
Let's go.

150
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:37,920
Gyah! Shari-gama!

151
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:46,540
Each to their own!

152
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,640
I'm not losing, no way!

153
00:08:49,980 --> 00:08:52,360
Such a waste!

154
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:53,840
Hey, how about this?

155
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,820
Hahaha! This is modern ninjutsu!

156
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:05,880
Using the Hot Tea Concealment Jutsu,

157
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:10,980
here's your return!

158
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,560
It's the Substitution Jutsu!

159
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,300
Grandpa

160
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:24,180
Volvo, quit the police right away

161
00:09:24,180 --> 00:09:26,060
and come back with that girl.

162
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:27,440
Why?

163
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:31,960
As my successor,
you will take on the ninja getup.

164
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,380
No, I'm not really...

165
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,300
What are you hesitating for?

166
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:39,220
If you become my successor,
you get the ninja getup and...

167
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:42,860
this 6,000-tsubo plot of land will be yours,
you know.

168
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:44,820
A 6,000-tsubo plot of land?

169
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:47,320
If not you, then who will inherit it?

170
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,340
Master...

171
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:50,760
Please make me your disciple.

172
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:52,120
What? You?

173
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:55,800
I was truly impressed by all
of your master's ninja arts.

174
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,880
I too wish to master the path of the ninja!

175
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:01,980
I see. That is admirable.

176
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:05,400
Your eye-blinding technique
from earlier shows real promise.

177
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:06,520
I'm honored!

178
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:08,700
Lord Ryo...

179
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:10,520
I wonder what he's thinking...

180
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:12,540
Very well,
I permit you to become my disciple.

181
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:13,420
Thank you very much.

182
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,160
Master, since you're going
to open a ninja school anyway,

183
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:21,560
why don't we also create a female ninja,
Kuno Sekka?

184
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,200
That's a fine idea.

185
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,460
You're quite fond of it yourself,
aren't you?

186
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,380
It's not like that.

187
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:35,040
They say those who've seen the same things are kindred spirits,
don't they?

188
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:39,640
Master, regarding that, I have a good idea.

189
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,400
Allow me to whisper.

190
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:53,800
This is undoubtedly a kunoichi!

191
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:55,940
This is a true kunoichi!

192
00:10:57,940 --> 00:10:59,000
What are you talking about!

193
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,380
Big ears to gather
intelligence on the enemy.

194
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:03,240
Chainmail to protect the body.

195
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:05,780
And a look that bewilders the enemy.

196
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:07,540
It's exactly a kunoichi, after all.

197
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:09,600
Well done, well done!

198
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:11,640
Not at all!

199
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:16,300
Can't be helped,
we'll go with this popular costume.

200
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:18,640
I liked the earlier one better, though.

201
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:21,160
I still feel it's too sexy.

202
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:25,060
Why are you taking pictures?

203
00:11:25,060 --> 00:11:27,480
It's for the brochure for the ninja school.

204
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:30,800
You know, the covers of travel
agency brochures and such

205
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,780
are usually pretty young women, right?

206
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:35,160
You need beauties to
draw in the young people.

207
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:35,760
I see.

208
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:39,180
Maria, lift your hem higher so
we can see more of your thighs!

209
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:40,060
Like this?

210
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:41,400
Nice!

211
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,940
Okay, next pose is...

212
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:45,500
Leave it to me.

213
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:48,120
Showing your shoulders
makes you look so seductive.

214
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,200
As expected of you, Master.
You really understand.

215
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:51,360
Let's go, Maria.

216
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:52,400
Yes.

217
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:57,620
Lean forward more, squeeze your arms in,
and show off your cleavage.

218
00:11:57,620 --> 00:12:03,120
Hey, why is your chest so flat?

219
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,200
Uh-oh.

220
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:07,540
Oh right, she was pretending to
be Volvo's fiancée, wasn't she?

221
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:10,400
Fine, I'll tell you the truth.

222
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,180
Maria is a man.

223
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:13,220
What?

224
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:15,520
Is she really a man?

225
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:16,660
Yes.

226
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:20,640
Hey, you deceived me, didn't you?

227
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:26,280
Yes.

228
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:28,980
Jodie-san.

229
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:32,060
Who exactly is this Jodie?

230
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:33,400
This one, this one right here.

231
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:36,080
What, you actually have a real girlfriend?

232
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:39,140
And she's a blonde, big-busted American.

233
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:41,360
Blonde with a great body, you say?

234
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:42,180
That's right, master.

235
00:12:42,180 --> 00:12:46,940
Why don't we use Jodie as the model
and shoot the brochure cover with her?

236
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:47,800
I see.

237
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:52,980
Great, great!

238
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:55,620
And if we pair her with Maria,

239
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:01,120
that'd be irresistible.

240
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:03,260
Right, then.

241
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:08,440
Since Jodie's aircraft carrier has
apparently arrived at Yokosuka port,

242
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:10,220
I'll just go and fetch her.

243
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:12,340
Right, I'm coming too!

244
00:13:12,340 --> 00:13:15,140
Why are you coming too, Grandpa?

245
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:18,340
She's practically my granddaughter-in-law,
after all.

246
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,640
She's going to be the model
for the ninja school brochure!

247
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:25,160
Alright! Everyone, let's go to Yokosuka!

248
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:26,820
W-wait, no way!

249
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:53,980
Phew.

250
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:55,040
What is that?!

251
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:56,940
A helicopter's coming!

252
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,180
Nobody told us there was a launch scheduled!

253
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:10,000
Dad!

254
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:12,740
What's going on?

255
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:16,360
I was passing by, so I came to see you.
It's been a while.

256
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:21,620
Well done, Jodie.

257
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:27,580
Don't shoot inside! Sorry about that.

258
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:32,080
Welcome to my residence.
Thank you for always looking after Jodie.

259
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:41,040
I've always heard the great rumors about you, that you distinguished yourself in countless wars and conflicts.
It's nothing much.

260
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:43,060
Ha ha

261
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:48,280
What a magnificent medal.

262
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:50,920
Looks like you caught me.

263
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:52,400
You showed it on purpose, though.

264
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:55,400
This one I received for my
service at the Ruby Front.

265
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:57,540
This one's from the Room War.

266
00:14:57,540 --> 00:15:00,960
This one's from the time of Operation Ultra,
the first one.

267
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,340
Another unauthorized helicopter is coming!

268
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:14,800
Jodie.

269
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:17,900
My darling.

270
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:20,720
Darling.

271
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:22,780
Long time no see.

272
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:27,620
Are you all right?

273
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:28,720
Yes.

274
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,640
Hey, Jodie.

275
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:33,020
Mr. Ryotsu, long time no see.

276
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:35,680
But Ryotsu, what's with that outfit?

277
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:37,500
I became a ninja's disciple.

278
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:38,740
Master.

279
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:45,340
Allow me to introduce

280
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:47,720
my master, Volvo's grandpa,

281
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:49,540
Mr. Saigo Koganemaru.

282
00:15:49,540 --> 00:15:51,260
Grandpa!

283
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:52,960
Nice to meet you. I'm Jodie.

284
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:55,340
The pleasure is mine.

285
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:57,900
So this beauty is the bride candidate?

286
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:58,460
Well, yes.

287
00:15:58,460 --> 00:15:59,980
Grandpa, you're a ninja?

288
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:01,640
Yes!

289
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:02,860
Take on a disciple.

290
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:05,900
Okay, everyone, move aside, move aside!

291
